2. Vector populations: Climate change can also affect the distribution and abundance of vector species, such as mosquitoes and ticks, which can transmit parasites to humans and animals. For example, changes in temperature and precipitation can lead to an increase in the abundance and distribution of mosquito vectors, potentially increasing the risk of vector-borne diseases.

