The oxygen content is calculated as:  
\[ \text{oxygen content} = \text{oxygen saturation} \times \text{haemoglobin} + \text{oxygen saturation} \times \text{blood volume} \times \text{oxygen saturation} \]  

Thus, the total oxygen delivery is:  
\[ \text{oxygen delivery} = \text{cardiac output} \times \left (\text{oxygen saturation} \times \text{haemoglobin} + \text{oxygen saturation} \times \text{oxygen saturation} \right ) \]  

The formula is calculated as:  
