Calculate the entropy change (J/mol K) of the given reaction. The molar entropies [J/K mol] are given in brackets after each substance.

\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} [91.2] + 3 \text{O}_2(g) [205.1] \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} [66.5] + 2 \text{SO}_2(g) [248.2] \]
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The change in entropy for the reaction is calculated as:
\[
\Delta G = \Delta H - T\Delta S
\]
Substituting the given molecular entropies:
\[
\Delta S = \sum_{ \text{products}} \Delta S_{\text{products}} - \sum( \text{Reactants} \times 1.1) \Delta S_{\text{Reactants}}
\]
Substituting the given molecular entropies:
\[
\Delta S = (2 \times 66.5 + 2 \times 248.2) - (2 \times 91.2 + 3 \times 205.1)
\]
\[
\Delta S = (122 + 494.4) - (192.4 + 510.3)
\]
\[
\Delta S = 616.4 - 602.7 = 11.7 \, \text{J/mol K}
\]

Thus, the change in entropy for the reaction is \(\boxed{11.7 \, \text{J/mol K}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

