\]

where:
- \(n\) is the number of equivalents of electrons transferred in the reaction.
- \(n_0</sub> is the Faraday number (\(96,455 \, \text{V} \cdot \text{C}^2/mol}).
- \(\Delta E\) is the standard free change of reaction (\DeltaG°), which can be calculated using the standard reduction potentials:

\[
\Delta E = E_ox -E_{red}
\]
where \(E_{ox}\) is the standard reduction potential of the cathode (oxidized species) and \(E_{red}\) is the standard reduction potential of the cathode (reduced species).

1. **Identify the half-actions and their standard reduction potentials:**
