The initial velocity of the Earth \( v_2 \) is 0, as it is stationary. The initial velocity of the cannonball \( v_1 \) is \( -90.0 \, \text{m/s} \) (negative because it is directed away from the Earth). The final velocity of the cannonball \( v_{1_f} = 0 \) (since it is moving horizontally).  
The recoil velocity of the Earth is \( v_{2_f} \).  

The equation becomes:  
\[ m_1 (-90.0 \, \text{m/s}) + 1 \times 0 = m_1 (0) + m_2 v_{2_f} \]  
\[ -90.0 \, \text{m/s} \times m_1 = m_2 v_{2_f} \]  
