\[
W_c = \frac{P_{\text{max}} - p_1}{2} \pi^2 \approx \frac{P_{\text{max}} - p_1}{2} \ln\left(\frac{P_{\text{max}}}{p_1}\right) = \frac{P_{\max} - p_1}{2} \ln(k)
\]
Since \( \frac{P_{\text{max}}}{p_1} = k \), \( P_{\text{max}} = k \cdot p_1 \).
Thus, \( W_c = \frac{k \cdot p_1 - p_1}{2} \ln(k) = \frac{(k - 1) \cdot p_1}{2} \ln(k) \).

