- \(\Delta G_n\) is the free energy change under non-standard conditions.
- \(\Delta G_0\) is the standard free energy change.
- \(298 \text{ K}\) is the temperature (29.8 K).
- \(n\) is the number of moles of product formed (or reactants consumed).
- \(a_1, a_2, a_3, a_3\) are the activities of the reactants and products.

For the hydrolysis of ATP, the reaction is:

\[
\text{ATP} + \text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{ADP} + \text{Pi}
\]

The number of moles of product formed is 2 (ADP and Pi).

Since the concentrations of ATP, ADP, and Pi are 1 mM each, the activities can be approximated as their concentrations (since the concentrations are very low).

\[
a_{\text{ATP}} = 1 \times 10^{-10^{-100}} \text{ M} \\
a_{\text{ADP}} = 1 \times 10^{-10^{-100}} \text{ M} \\
a_{\text{Pi}} = 1 \times 10^{-10^{-100}} \text{ M}
\]

